# Architect Gate

Runs during `/architect` after refactor. Final automated hardening before gated `/code-review` (stage 9). Human gate 3 is merge at stage 12, not this step.

## When to run

After `/refactor` passes all refactor gates.

## Scripts

From repository root:

```powershell
dotnet stryker --config-file stryker-config.json
dotnet test
# Only when acceptance tests exist (opt-in for now):
./scripts/run-gherkin-mutation.ps1
```

Ensure tools are restored: `dotnet tool restore`

## Thresholds

- **Stryker mutation score:** at or above `gates.mutation.threshold` in `harness.yml` (default **80%**), rendered into `stryker-config.json` by `install.ps1`.

  A surviving mutant means the mutated line's behaviour is unasserted. **Fix the test, never the threshold** — lowering the number is accepting the defect, not resolving it. Route survivors through `mutation-analyst`, which separates real gaps from equivalent mutants.
- **Gherkin mutation** *(only when `specs/<feature>/acceptance/*.feature` exists)*: zero survivors — mutated scenarios must cause test failures. Acceptance tests are opt-in for now; skip this check when there are none.

## Survivor routing

| Failure | Re-run |
|---|---|
| Stryker survivor | `/implement` or `/refactor` (add/strengthen tests) |
| Gherkin mutation survivor *(if acceptance tests exist)* | `/implement` (strengthen bindings) |
| Full suite failure | Fix and re-run architect gates |

## Do not

Mark feature complete or suggest opening a PR until architect gates, `/code-review` (stage 9), and `/ship-review` (stage 10) have all completed. Human gate 3 is merge at stage 12, after the PR.
